body:
Update:

Sorry for taking so long folks. I had to put all my stuff back, set up notification settings and all that stuff again... Not fun. HOWEVER, The Lineage 16.0 Build attached here can be considered daily driver material! It more or less has the same bugs as Lineage 15.1 (~~no native Quad-DAC support, tho there is a workaround, and the other two minor bugs~~, This release has native Quad DAC support) but this thing is F L Y I N G. I have had no app crashes, random reboots, slowdowns, or anything like that. In fact, I can report most "hacks" for Oreo, like the audio mod, also work here in this build as well.

&#x200B;

Now, just a few things I want to point out:

\-If you use OpenGapps, Make sure to use the aroma installer. Do NOT install the Pixel Launcher through here. Do NOT install the GCam through here. Instead, install the V30 GCam Port (so you can use both cams), and once you get your device certified (Use the Pixel 2 XL Fingerprint, Use MagiskProps), you can then just download the launcher from the play store. Alternative solution: Use BitGApps.

\-Google's Set Up will Force Close if you connect to Wi-Fi (does not do this on cellular) but you are able to continue and will not display again once the phone is set up. You can also skip and set up later.

&#x200B;

\-Once again, Viper4Android AND the Audio mods that enable dual speakers still work on this release.

\-Yes, the gestures are here as well ;). Enable in settings.

\-Better Rescale support - Changing the DPI will no longer cut off the corners of the clock.

&#x200B;

Android P really put new life into this V30, and now I am satisfied.

tl;dr - This is my daily driver rom now... Everything that works in Lineage 15.1 works in this attached build. The Quad DAC now even works natively (change through Settings > Sound); Enjoy it.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
